  "preamble": "Loss of the labio-velar approximant [w]. English lost it in initial wr- and after s in sword. Most Ancient Greek dialects lost digamma ϝ [w] entirely, and Japanese lost /w/ before every vowel except a. Initial *w was dropped in Australian initial-dropping languages, e.g. Uradhi anta- < Proto-Paman *wanta- 'put'.",
